Subject: [PATCH] BOOTSPEED-2: the three boot hot spots the sampler found
 (write-through ini + production-record titles)

Boot samples 20260929 (bootsample_..._16644 / _12284): 68-98 s before the op-log START line; >70 % in
 (1) W906_SecurityJamBoot, 30-46 s: D:\HT9045\Error\English\ is missing on this machine, so JAM0000.dat can never be
     created and golden's "build it once" loop runs every boot: ~210,000 failed opens (on-access scanner 0.1-0.35 ms
     each) + a never-read in-memory mirror growing to ~23,000 keys;
 (2) TMyProductionRecord ctor x 37,800 (InitialMotorParameter), 13-21 s: five all-literal titles rebuilt every time;
 (3) WriteLastDataFile x 4, 6-14 s: ~290 whole-file rewrites of config.ini each, with the bytes already on disk.

vclcompat/IniFiles.cpp (write-through TIniFile only; TMemIniFile unchanged):
 - W906_IniProbe: GetFileAttributesA first; only FILE_NOT_FOUND / PATH_NOT_FOUND skip an open that would fail anyway
   (a missing directory also skips the "wb" create that cannot succeed). Everything else opens as before.
 - WriteString no longer mirrors into store_ when writing through (store_ is read only by the Mem variant).
 - identical result bytes -> W906_IniTouchSame stamps LastWriteTime (what kernel32 does, measured) instead of
   truncate + rewrite; declines for any attribute other than plain ARCHIVE.
 - W906_IniApplyFast = W906IniApply's bytes in one pass; the old engine kept as W906_Win32ProfileApplyRef.
Public/MyProductionRecord.cpp: the five titles are function-local statics, copied (same bytes).

Verified (scratch builds only): IniFiles 50/50, IniFiles_Win32Diff 3,027 cases vs kernel32 0 mismatches,
IniFiles_Win32ReadDiff PASS, old-vs-new 404,970 cases 0 differences (re-run 21:3x), 9-case behaviour table identical.
Known residual: a same-value write into a file another process holds open without write sharing now moves its
LastWriteTime (the old path failed to open it); contents identical either way.

